{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n`src/rebar/_signing_hmac.py` (276 LOC) keeps key custody, payload canonicalisation, `compute_signature`, and `verify_record` alive so the dispatcher can still verify a symmetric scheme that mints nothing: the 3,883 live SIGNATURE events on this tracker are all Ed25519 op-certs, and `sign_manifest` (library; CLI `rebar sign` at `src/rebar/signing.py:353-391`; MCP `sign_manifest` at `src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py:502-515`) mints only through `mint_opcert_record` (`signing.py:218`). A record of an op-cert kind already reads NOT-certified (`_hmac_opcert_not_certified`, `_signing_hmac.py:259-276`), but `REBAR_SIGNING_KEY` and `<tracker>/.signing-key` are still read on every verify (`signing.py:157,268,278`), `rebar init` still writes a secret nobody uses (`src/rebar/_commands/init.py:488-495`), and the generic non-op-cert HMAC path (`signing.py:156-158`) is reachable by no producer. The 688 folded SNAPSHOTs carrying HMAC entries (1,124 entries on closed or deleted tickets, 1 on an open ticket) must keep reducing and rendering; they must simply verify as `unsigned`. The reducer folds `attestations[kind]` dicts verbatim (`src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py:556-559`) and never imports `_signing_hmac`. Three HMAC readers remain (`signing.py:151-158`, `signing.py:268,278`, `src/rebar/_engine_support/validate.py:88-91`); no doctor or fsck module reads the key file. `foreign_key` and `unknown_scheme` remain live op-cert and registry verdicts (`src/rebar/_opcert_verify.py:282,293,308`; `src/rebar/attest/registry.py:108`), so the `verify_signature_result.schema.json:17` enum and `types.py:361-371` Literal do not change. Operator decision (2026-09-06): retire fully. Cites are on origin/main 360d504f5ceb.\n\n## Approach\n1. Replacement function in `src/rebar/signing.py`, replacing the import block at `signing.py:40-51`:\n```python\nLEGACY_HMAC_ALGORITHM = \"HMAC-SHA256\"   # recognised on read only; never minted\nHMAC_RETIRED_ON = \"2026-09\"\n\ndef retired_scheme_verdict(record: dict | None) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Uniform NOT-certified verdict for any non-envelope SIGNATURE record. Same base keys\n    as the op-cert verdict (_opcert_verify.py:225-241) so compute_validity /\n    signature_findings / plan_review_status read it unchanged; never raises.\"\"\"\n    record = record if isinstance(record, dict) else {}\n    raw = record.get(\"manifest\")\n    manifest = raw if isinstance(raw, list) else []\n    key_id = record.get(\"key_id\")\n    legacy = bool(record.get(\"signature\")) or record.get(\"algorithm\") == LEGACY_HMAC_ALGORITHM\n    return {\n        \"manifest\": manifest, \"step_count\": len(manifest),\n        \"algorithm\": record.get(\"algorithm\"),\n        \"key_id\": key_id if isinstance(key_id, str) else None,\n        \"signed_at\": record.get(\"signed_at\"), \"head_sha\": record.get(\"head_sha\"),\n        \"verified_at_sha\": verified_at_sha_from_manifest(manifest) or record.get(\"verified_at_sha\"),\n        \"rebar_version\": rebar_version_from_manifest(manifest), \"trust_basis\": None,\n        \"verified\": False, \"verdict\": \"unsigned\",\n        \"reason\": (f\"legacy HMAC scheme retired ({HMAC_RETIRED_ON}); re-run the gate to mint an op-cert\"\n                   if legacy else \"ticket has no signature\"),\n    }\n```\n2. `verify_attestation_record(record, ticket_id, *, kind=None, repo_root=None)` (`signing.py:119-158`): drop the `key` kwarg and the `attestation_kind` import; body becomes envelope -> `verify_opcert_record(...)`, else `retired_scheme_verdict(record)`. `OPCERT_KINDS` (`signing.py:115`) stays (imported by `src/rebar/_commands/remote_cert.py:22`, `src/rebar/opcert_service/jobs.py:32`).\n3. `_resolve_and_reduce` (`signing.py:246-278`) returns `(resolved, state)`; `verify_signature` and `verify_attestations` (`signing.py:325-349`) stop passing `key=`. Delete the legacy render branch in `sign_cli` (`signing.py:384-390`, reads `record['key_id']`/`['signature']`, unreachable). Rewrite the module docstring (`signing.py:1-22`) and `__all__` (`signing.py:74-109`): remove `ALGORITHM`, `PAYLOAD_VERSION`, `_NO_KEY`, `_canonical_payload`, `_generate_key_file`, `_hmac_opcert_not_certified`, `compute_signature`, `key_fingerprint`, `signing_key`, `verify_record`; add `retired_scheme_verdict`, `LEGACY_HMAC_ALGORITHM`, `HMAC_RETIRED_ON`.\nSteps 4 to 10 (validate.py, init.py, kept read-compat, the prose sweep, docs, baselines, ADR amendments) and the exact test delete/rewrite/touch lists are in this ticket's first comment.\n\n## Scope\n`src/rebar/_signing_hmac.py` (delete); `src/rebar/signing.py`; `src/rebar/_engine_support/validate.py`; `src/rebar/_commands/init.py`; the nine prose files in step 7; `src/rebar/schemas/sign_result.schema.json`; `src/rebar/schemas/verify_signature_result.schema.json`; the ten docs in step 8; `docs/adr/0044-asymmetric-attestation-substrate.md`; `docs/adr/0049-opcert-asymmetric.md`; `docs/release-notes.md`; `tests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json` (regenerated); tests below. Out of scope: `.gitignore` (only `infra/compose/*signing-key` lines, unrelated), `infra/**` (`MCP_HMAC_SIGNING_KEY` and the SSO cookie HMAC are different secrets), `docs/security.md` (no mention), `_present.py`, the `ticket_state.signature` mirror.\n\n## Testing\nHappy: `pytest tests/unit/test_hmac_retirement.py tests/unit/test_signing.py tests/unit/test_signing_module_split.py tests/unit/test_hmac_opcert_removal_8f1d.py tests/unit/test_opcert_producer_seam_8d8e.py tests/interfaces/lifecycle -q`; `python scripts/gen_api_surface.py --check`; `python scripts/gen_env_registry.py --check`; `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check`; `rebar init` in a temp repo followed by `test -e .tickets-tracker/.signing-key` fails. Edge: non-list `manifest` gives `step_count 0` and `unsigned`; a `signature`-bearing record whose `manifest[0]` is `custom: x` gives `unsigned` (no generic path); a map with HMAC `plan-review` plus a fresh op-cert `completion-verifier` gives `unsigned` and `certified` respectively; `verify_attestation_record(None, id)` gives `reason == \"ticket has no signature\"`. `make verify` before push.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `src/rebar/_signing_hmac.py` is absent and `git grep -E 'signing_key\\(|REBAR_SIGNING_KEY|compute_signature|verify_record\\b' -- src` prints nothing (asserted by `test_hmac_retirement.py::test_no_hmac_readers_remain`).\n- [ ] `verify_attestation_record` has no `key` parameter and `retired_scheme_verdict` is exported; `python scripts/gen_api_surface.py --check` exits 0.\n- [ ] The 003d-shaped SNAPSHOT fixture reduces, renders, and verifies `unsigned` with the retired reason on the CLI, on MCP `verify_signature`, and on `plan_review_status` (tests a to c pass).\n- [ ] `rebar init` no longer writes `.signing-key` and `.signing-key` remains in the tracker `.gitignore` (test in `tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py`).\n- [ ] `signature_findings` emits nothing for a store of HMAC-only records (test d).\n- [ ] `docs/env-vars.md` has no `REBAR_SIGNING_KEY` row; ADR 0044 and 0049 carry the amendment paragraphs; the release note is present and `tests/unit/test_hmac_opcert_removal_8f1d.py::test_migration_doc_present_and_documented` asserts the \"Retirement (2026-09)\" heading.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0.\n\nRelease note (BREAKING, pre-1.0): the legacy HMAC-SHA256 signing scheme is retired. `REBAR_SIGNING_KEY` and `<tracker>/.signing-key` are no longer read (`rebar init` stops creating the file; delete yours); every SIGNATURE record without a DSSE `envelope` (all attestations minted before 2026-07-15) now verifies `unsigned` with reason `legacy HMAC scheme retired (2026-09); re-run the gate to mint an op-cert`, no longer `unknown_scheme` or `foreign_key`; closed tickets are unaffected; an open ticket holding one needs one `rebar review-plan`; `rebar.signing.{signing_key, key_fingerprint, compute_signature, verify_record, ALGORITHM, PAYLOAD_VERSION}` are removed from the library surface and `verify_attestation_record` loses its `key` parameter."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788838433930607001,"uuid":"3ae4296c-7b91-49e4-aabf-f3ea7e5bbf36"}